  "Question": "Represent the hypotenuse of a right triangle by \\(c\\) and the area by \\(A.\\) The altitude on the hypotenuse is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac Ac\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{2A}{c}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac A{2c}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{A^2}{c}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac A{c^2}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The hypotenuse can serve as the base in the triangle area formula. Let \\(h\\) be the altitude perpendicular to this base. Then\n\\[\nA=\\frac12 ch.\n\\]\nSince the hypotenuse has positive length, \\(c>0\\). Multiplying by \\(2\\) and dividing by \\(c\\) gives\n\\[\nh=\\frac{2A}{c}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
